module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.Coherent
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Noetherian
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.FunctionField
public import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Module

/-! # Clearing denominators for a local map from a closed structure module

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 01YB and 01YE, the ideal-power extension step.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u
open CategoryTheory
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- A local map from a closed structure module extends after restricting its source
by a nonzero ideal on the integral closed subscheme. No injectivity is assumed or
asserted. Agreement holds on the entire given open, not just on the generic stalk.
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 01YB (extension from ideal powers), as used in the last
paragraph of Tag 01YE, with the affine closed-pushforward calculation of Tag 01QY.
(blueprint: lem-pc-local-closed-ideal-map-extension)

Proof: let I be the reduced ideal of the closed complement of U. The closed
pushforward H = i_*O_W is coherent: on each affine open Spec A in X its sections
are the quotient A/K defining W, hence a finite A-module. The coherent target G
is quasi-coherent. Tag 01YB extends the given map from H|U to G|U to a global map
I^n H -> G for some n, agreeing with the given map on U after the product inclusion.
On Spec A, write B = A/K and let L be the ideal of I. Then I^n H has sections
L^n B, the ideal generated by the image of L^n in B. These ideals commute with
localization and define a quasi-coherent ideal J on W; equivalently J is the nth
power of the extended ideal I O_W, with J = O_W if n = 0. The affine identifications
assemble to an isomorphism i_*J -> I^n H commuting with inclusions into H. Compose
this isomorphism with the extended map to obtain alpha. Since the generic image
lies in U, I is the unit ideal there. Thus J has full nonzero generic stalk, so
J is not the zero ideal. Restricting the commuting inclusion diagram to U gives
the displayed equality. This works also for the zero local map and for U = X;
in the latter case one may take J = O_W and alpha equal to the given map. -/
theorem local_closed_ideal_map_extension
    {X W : Scheme.{u}} [IsNoetherian X]
    (i : W ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [IsIntegral W]
    (G : X.Modules) (hG : RingedSpace.IsCoherent X.toRingedSpace G)
    (U : X.Opens) (hx : i.base (genericPoint W) ∈ U)
    (φ : (restrictFunctor U.ι).obj
        ((pushforward i).obj (SheafOfModules.unit W.ringCatSheaf)) ⟶
      (restrictFunctor U.ι).obj G) :
    ∃ (J : W.IdealSheafData), J ≠ ⊥ ∧
      ∃ (α : (pushforward i).obj J.toModules ⟶ G),
        (restrictFunctor U.ι).map α =
          (restrictFunctor U.ι).map ((pushforward i).map J.toModulesι) ≫ φ := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
